id: pm-gh1583
title: "GH-1583: recognize concrete private home paths through bounded shared normalization"
description: "The public detector-coverage report exposes platform and representation gaps in shared preflight. Recognize concrete private home coordinates at one shared matching boundary while preserving portable references, redacted diagnostics and existing guard modes. This is detection-only and does not make direct SDK persistence automatically guarded."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:security",privacy,sdk,secret-guard
created_at: "2026-10-25T07:07:40.489Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T11:36:59.890Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-25T11:23:16.611Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T11:23:16.611Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Recognize native POSIX, macOS, Windows, UNC and file-URL private home paths in the shared detector; Use bounded percent, escaped-slash and documented Unicode views while retaining original repository line locations; Keep portable aliases and non-private paths clear and preserve off, advise, block, force and scan-failure semantics; Return only safe typed normalization provenance and deterministic redacted findings; Prove pre-fix failure and legitimate controls through shared SDK/repository matching and guarded adapters"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "SDK preflight and repository scanning share platform, namespace, file-URL and bounded representation matching. Findings retain redacted provenance and whole-leaf incomplete status, escape scans are linear, portable references and guard modes remain compatible, and the approved legacy prefixes are removed through attributed SDK audit operations."
expected_result: "Concrete private profile coordinates receive consistent redacted findings across documented representations, with explicit incomplete inspection and preserved legitimate workflows; tracked context and history remain valid."
actual_result: "197 linked assertions, four strict type projects, full canonical static quality, SDK surface and documentation checks pass. Node and Bun each pass 16 compiled SDK checks. The approved ten prefix replacements in seven records preserve all other event and current-item content, every affected chain verifies, full tracker validation has zero errors or warnings, graph and record assurance pass, and the tracked-file secret scan is clear. Prior pushed-head full CI coverage is exact 100 percent; final-head hosted validation is required before merge."
