comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T07:07:40.489Z","harness:codex","Intake for GitHub issue1583. Live request searches and open/in-progress inventories plus the complete3106-item corpus found no existing owner for representation normalization. Full live predecessor metadata/history confirms pm-pim7 delivered guarded preflight and pm-wwooxx delivered shared rule inventory: those completed scopes remain intact. New work extends concrete private-path coverage, preserves portable aliases and explicitly bounds the detector guarantee. Use only synthetic evidence from the already-public report."
  "2026-10-25T07:19:27.577Z","harness:codex","Independent regression baseline:34 failures and25 controls pass across59 cases before the fix. The read-only boundary investigator confirms shared SDK/repository matching is required, original source lines must survive normalization, routing paths and portable current-user aliases must remain usable, and direct SDK writes are not universally guarded. Keep existing configured modes and explicit override semantics. Recognize named-account references separately from current-user aliases and report bounded incomplete inspection conservatively rather than returning an unqualified clean result."
  "2026-10-25T07:46:53.866Z","harness:codex","The one independent candidate review identified relative-path false positives and a missing bidi control. Both are corrected with regression cases. The shared matcher remains source-executable before a build and lazy for SDK callers. Current-user and named aliases remain literal to preserve portable project context, while concrete platform paths and bounded normalized views are covered. Expanded repository scanning exposes six pre-existing historical records: the prepared SDK dry-run replaces eight coordinate prefixes, preserves relative suffixes, verifies every chain with zero mismatches and confirms no source files changed. Recovery copies are retained. Explicit user approval for the audited history rewrite is pending; no redaction, force override or historical waiver has been applied."
  "2026-10-25T08:10:26.529Z","harness:codex","The complete first source run passed11318 tests but one packed-consumer test could not resolve npm under the local Homebrew runtime, so no full coverage receipt was produced. Restored the documented per-command Node module environment without changing tests or product behavior and started a full rerun. Focused coverage exercises every edited shared-matcher branch; its only uncovered line is the pre-existing non-string-leaf return exercised elsewhere by the complete suite. The focused linked suite, strict types, SDK surface update and documentation links pass. Historical redaction approval remains pending and no history rewrite has occurred."
  "2026-10-25T08:33:02.165Z","harness:codex","The complete source suite passed11319 tests with3 skips and exact100/100/100/100 coverage. Subsequent parser checks confirmed two additional equivalent forms: backslash file URLs and repeated separators. Added explicit profile-root handling and controls distinguishing URL authorities from local paths; all163 focused cases pass. The full coverage receipt predates these final regex-only additions, so hosted coverage must verify the final head. Historical rewrite approval remains pending; no history has been redacted."
  "2026-10-25T08:38:38.635Z","harness:codex","Final isolated redaction rehearsal passes for seven legacy records, with ten coordinate-prefix replacements, zero remaining findings and valid recomputed history chains. This adds the audit shorthand record pm-xk39 and the Windows-root spelling in pm-s5pe to the earlier plan. Every authoritative source file remains unchanged. The retained recovery copy and exact dry-run scope are prepared; applying the real audited rewrite still requires explicit approval under repository policy. Full static checks are running after the complexity-preserving matcher extraction."
  "2026-10-25T08:51:42.631Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence:163 linked assertions pass after the URL/separator cases and normalization-helper extraction; all four strict type projects, source lint/duplication/docstrings/export/dependency gates, SDK surface and import/transport budgets pass. Tracker context, graph composition and record integrity pass after recording confidence and explicit related-record edges. The existing mutation gate passes345 killed plus7 equivalent, zero failures. Latest pm-changelog2026.10.25 installs, generates2758 eligible closed-work rows unchanged and passes check; contracts, documentation links and this history chain pass. The complete predecessor coverage receipt is11319 passed/3 skipped/exact100%; final-head hosted coverage is required. Repository secret scan still reports20 matches across seven legacy records. Authoritative legacy history remains untouched pending the final seven-record approval. Prepare a draft PR for external review; do not close the item or merge through the failing secret gate."
  "2026-10-25T09:15:31.677Z","harness:codex","Draft PR1584 review identifies three concrete candidates for correction: UNC share prefixes before Users, incomplete inspection on a later string-leaf line, and CodeQL alert52 for polynomial matching of backslash runs. Reproduce each at the shared boundary and retain legitimate controls. Preserve lazy first-hit behavior for credential rules while carrying conservative whole-leaf inspection status for home paths. The full canonical static command now passes on the initial pushed head. The seven-record history redaction remains unapproved and unchanged."
  "2026-10-25T09:57:22.608Z","harness:codex","Review remediation is complete locally: shared profiles include ordinary and spaced UNC shares; incomplete status survives later lines and the same line, including a first coordinate revealed on the final pass. Credential rules retain lazy first-hit matching. Escape views consume whole unmatched backslash runs and residual detection requires one slash, removing the confirmed polynomial route from CodeQL report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/security/code-scanning/52. The original built candidate exceeded a5-second bound on200000 backslashes; corrected Node and Bun public-SDK consumers pass11 checks each. Final focused/linked suite passes179 tests; strict types, full canonical static quality, SDK surface, import/transport budgets, tracker/graph/history assurance, mutation and documentation checks pass. Full preceding review candidate passed11343 tests/3 skips/exact100 percent before the final five sibling regressions, so exact final-head hosted coverage remains required. CodSpeed reports0.2 percent aggregate change with an explicit different-runner warning on unchanged pagination implementations; no causal regression or threshold waiver is claimed. Fresh observability passes with0 critical/high issues,4.95 percent telemetry errors within the unchanged6 percent bound,0 missing codes,345 paired starts/finishes and0 pairing anomalies; physical queue0 with1 consumer. Today native scheduled run40174049913 verified the earlier immutable v2026.10.25 publication without another release. All29 open GitHub issues have PM links. Final real secret scan still finds20 matches in the same seven legacy records; final isolated redaction rehearsal clears all and verifies every chain. Approval remains pending, and no authoritative legacy history was redacted."
  "2026-10-25T10:24:47.727Z","harness:codex","The second full review confirms the earlier UNC-share and whole-leaf fixes, and fresh CodeQL analysis clears the polynomial finding. One concrete remaining route uses the Windows extended UNC namespace. Microsoft documentation confirms both question-mark and period device prefixes, with UNC, drive and volume forms: https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/standard/io/file-path-formats . Add the documented namespace family at the same shared boundary and preserve ordinary device/URL controls. The final seven-record history plan remains unapproved and unchanged."
  "2026-10-25T11:23:15.821Z","harness:codex","User explicitly approved the final seven-record, ten-prefix plan. The public SDK applied exactly that scope without force, retaining recovery copies and appending one attributed history-redact marker per stream. Independent comparison verifies every original event payload and current item text differs only by the approved replacements; record-hash sealing and reanchor metadata retain the original hashes. Full storage/history validation has zero errors or warnings, graph and record assurance pass, and tracked-file secret scanning now reports zero findings. The final matcher also covers both documented Windows device prefixes with UNC, drive and volume forms, including the real Node fileURLToPath namespace URI transition. Namespace baseline was five failures and five compatibility passes; final linked suite passes 197 tests, all four strict type projects and full canonical static quality pass. Compiled Node and Bun public-SDK consumers each pass 16 checks. Previous pushed-head full CI coverage is exactly 100/100/100/100, with final-head CI and review required before merge. Closeout, generated changelog and the approved audit migration will land together through the existing PR."
  "2026-10-25T11:36:59.890Z","harness:codex","The latest official pm-changelog 2026.10.25 generator and check both pass with 2759 eligible rows. The security entry appears exactly once under Unreleased alongside the three earlier delivered items, and is absent from the immutable v2026.10.25 publication. Final post-close tracker validation, context/graph/record assurance and defect-evidence checks pass; no implementation claim remains active."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T11:36:59.243Z","harness:codex","Keep shared policy modules executable by pre-build repository tooling. A first match does not prove inspection completed elsewhere in the same leaf. Consume unmatched escape runs as units rather than retrying required suffixes. Preserve original source locations and return transformation identities instead of sensitive values. For approved history redaction, verify both the rewritten chains and exact non-hash content against retained recovery copies."
